WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:14.770
Start with the small repeat, then walk on to the large designs. In the ceremonial kind, guides say, the design runs across the seams as one picture, and the motifs gather below the obi and at the left shoulder.

2
00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:26.650
Robes of this age are rare. Koide explains why: the kosode was a thing to be worn out. So she counted robes in paintings instead, nearly a thousand of them.

3
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:33.970
Her finding is that no style stood alone. Each borrowed elements from the others, and in exchange made the next.

4
00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:44.810
Koide ties the Kanbun style to a wider public. As the shogun's order settled, townspeople came to enjoy the kosode, in quality and in number.

5
00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:59.870
Today the code is read less closely. Asked about the flowers on her own furisode, one young woman told Becke: flowers are flowers, right? She had chosen by colour. In the next room, the flat picture meets a body.
